    "path": "/longContentPages/0",
    "raw": "FrackinUniverse adds a large amount of armors (and foods) and enhances some older ones, allowing for a greater variety of playstyles. These can be very useful through gameplay and provide exceptionally useful benefits!\n\n^yellow;Set Bonus Inheritance^reset;: As an important note, armors that are used to craft other armors can still be used to complete armor set bonuses for sets that were used in the crafting chain, so partially upgrading your set is still viable.\n\n^orange;Stats^reset; : Vanilla players may notice there are more than they are used to, and even the ones they are used to have different ranges. FU presents a wider variety of armor classes to spice up your play, and does the same with food.\n\nIf you are more interested in damage, pick up Power Armor or Hyper Power Armor to trade defensive stats for offensive ones. Alternatively, pick up Tank or Hyper Tank sets to outlast your enemy. They come in melee OR ranged! Fighting not quite your thing? Pick up an Exploration oriented set, and be at home in your environment! You're guaranteed to locate a set that suits your playstyle somewhere out there!\n\n^orange;Resistances^reset; : Many armors in FU come with inherent resistances. Many biome weather effects will simply stop affecting you once you hit an appropriate amount, and various enemy attacks will do less damage. Nifty, right? It gets better; upgrade your armor, and those resistances will increase!\n\n^orange;Bonuses^reset; : Most are increases to your stats, plenty are conditional.\nAny that say ^green;+value^reset; are typically additive increases. It can be a little confusing, however. As example: if it gives +^green;3^reset;% Crit Chance it increases your crit chance by a flat 3%, but if it says +^green;3^reset;% Energy Regen, that's 3% of your base. The easiest way to remember is to ask yourself...does it have a base of 0? If so, it likely is like Crit Chance! If a bonus says x^green;1.3^reset;, or ^green;More^reset;, that's a multiplier on the value you currently have. Have 1000% Damage somehow? 100% More (or 2x) would make it 2000%! Small note: Regen is usually per second.\n\nOf course, some bonuses have hidden components we couldn't easily include, for tooltip space.\n Additionally, there are some other phrase uses to note. If a set bonus states that it grants immunity to ^green;ALL^reset; of a related effect, that typically means all biome weather ^orange;as well as^reset; specific status effects related to that element. For heat, that includes burning and even lava! For radiation, that includes rad-burn.\nAs a small side-note, some terms or symbols are used loosely. If you see a bonus with x/y, that means the bonuses are different based on how their conditions are met. For weapons, this means how many of that type. If you see something like (Machine) Pistols, that means the bonus applies to Machine Pistols OR Pistols. This is typically done for tooltip space.\n\n^cyan;Mining Sets^reset; :\n Mining laser sets grant a lot more mining laser damage...but that bonus is reduced significantly if you are pairing them with something else. Using a mining laser with a pistol, as example: 2x Mining Laser Damage becomes 1.25x.\n^orange;Colors^reset;: Colors are important in identifying and understanding bonuses. To start with, set bonuses are identified by a ^yellow;^reset;, while a ^green;^reset; is only visible in crafting interfaces to display resistances. If a bonus stat is ^green;GREEN^reset;, that means it is a good thing. ^red;RED^reset; means it is a bad thing. ^cyan;Cyan^reset; is for bonuses that are binary. They typically do not stack with similar effects. This will be especially apparent with various foods...so choose carefully. It is worth noticing that there is ONE exception to the rules regarding colors: Glow. If you see Glow in a color, that is usually the color of the glow effect.\n\n^orange;Special Bonuses^reset; : Some sets have special bonuses that don't really display much information due to lack of space, an unfortunate limitation of the game. Here, some bonuses will be explained.\n\n^cyan;Adaptive Armor^reset;: Multiplies the wearer's total defense based on current health percentage, scaling between the left value at 20% health and the right value at 100% health.\n\n^cyan;Auto-Medic^reset;: More complicated than ordinary regeneration, this effect will restore more health per second at the cost of an equal percentage of energy. It will also decrease energy regen and increase energy regen lock-out multiplicatively at 2x the heal percent.\n\n^cyan;Thorns^reset;: a nova of thorns when hit, ^cyan;Fire Burst^reset; makes a nova of fire instead.\n\n^cyan;Summons Minions^reset;: summons short-lived allies to fight alongside you or distract enemies. These minions scale based on the lowest armor's tier, so upgrading it is essential! Upgrade ALL of the pieces.\n\n^cyan;Life/Energy Shell^reset;: Gain damage absorption (shell) which scales based on your maximum resources (health, energy) to protect your health. Regenerates quickly if you haven't taken damage recently. ^cyan;Shell Immunities^reset; are granted only while the shell holds. The numbers specified refer to, in order: The capacity of the shield relative to the resource, the regeneration rate, and the delay upon taking damage before it begins regenerating. Special note: Due to balance concerns, Energy Shell has a minimum lockout time of 0.5 seconds, and a maximum regen rate of 50% per second.\n\n^cyan;Gravity Normalization^reset;: Personal gravity too low? Up it goes. Too high? Down instead. Exception: Zero-gravity.\n\n^cyan;Vital Power^reset; and ^cyan;Juggernaut^reset;: these effects are set bonus exclusive, and quite powerful; they grant one stat based on a percent of another. Vital power grants power as life, Juggernaut grants life as power.\n\n^cyan;Undying Resolve^reset;: increases Protection as your life gets lower, up to the stated amount, while ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; grants HP Regen instead. If a set grants either, it will grant ^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset; to your pet.\n\n^cyan;Dark Commander^reset;/^cyan;Beast Master^reset;: Increases Damage, Protection, HP and Speed of your pets (both) and crew (Dark Commander) by the listed percent, increases their jump ability by half of that, and regenerates HP at a sixth of that amount per second.\n\n^cyan;Capturenaut^reset;: Increases pet count by 1, plus an additional 1 per 2 tiers (up to +2) of the lowest equipped set piece. Grants an additional +1 if using alongside the back item. This means a fully upgraded set will allow up to 5 additional pets!\n\n^red;Wretchel Toxicity^reset;: Ingesting Wretchel reduces core stats and healing received, and drains health over time. These effects increase in severity the more you consume in a short time frame, as well as while your health is critically low. It will ^red;KILL^reset; you, if you are careless.\n\n^cyan;Charisma^reset;: Your ability to bargain with Traders at space stations. The higher your charisma, the better the deal (and fatter your bank balance!)\n\n\n\n^cyan;Pet/Crew Stat Inheritance^reset;:\nOverall scaling is as follows: HP, directly from your character, rather than just equipped armor. Protection: applied as a multiplier to HP via a specific formula. Damage: directly from character sheet. Health Regen: Inherits as a flat amount, except in special cases (^cyan;Immortal Resolve^reset;, effects not covered by FU, etc.). If you have 100 health and 10% HP Regen, it will grant your pet 10 HP per second. If a stat isn't here, a pet most likely does not inherit it.\n^yellow;Special notes^reset;: Be mindful when taking powerful buffs like ^cyan;Glass Cannon^reset;, as it will reduce their health noticeably.\n",
    "value": "富兰克林的宇宙新增了大量护甲（及食物）并强化了部分原有物品，极大丰富了游戏风格选择。这些装备在游戏中极为实用，能提供卓越的增益效果！\n\n^yellow;套装奖励继承^reset;：重要提示：用于合成其他护甲的护甲，仍可激活其所属制作链中的套装奖励。因此即使部分升级套装，奖励依然有效。\n\n^orange;属性^reset;：原版玩家可能会注意到，护甲类型比以往更多，甚至熟悉类型的数值范围也有所不同。FU 通过更丰富的护甲和食物类别，为您的游戏体验增添多样性。\n\n\n若您更注重伤害，可选择力量或超力量护甲，以防御属性换取攻击属性；或选用坦克、超坦克套装，以持久战压制敌人。这些护甲分近战与远程版本！若不擅长战斗？可选探索向套装，在各种环境中从容行动！您一定能找到适合自己风格的套装！\n\n^orange;抗性^reset;：FU 中许多护甲自带固有抗性。一旦抗性达到相应数值，多种生物群系天气效果将不再对您产生影响，各类敌人攻击造成的伤害也会降低。很实用吧？还有更好的：升级护甲后，这些抗性还会进一步提升！\n\n^orange;奖励^reset;：多数奖励为属性提升，且不少附带触发条件。\n带 ^green;+^reset; 的数值通常为加算，但需注意区分。例如：装备提供 ^green;+3^reset;% 暴击率时，暴击率直接增加 3%；若描述为 ^green;+3^reset;% 能量回复，则指基于基础回复值提升 3%。简易判断方法是自问：该属性是否以 0 为基数？若是，则加成方式同暴击率。若奖励显示为 x^green;1.3^reset; 或 ^green;更多^reset;，则为当前值的乘算。例如原有 1000% 伤害，100% 更多（即 2 倍）后将变为 2000%！注：生命回复通常以秒为单位。\n\n为节省提示栏空间，部分奖励含有未列明的隐藏效果，有待您自行探索。\n另需注意以下短语用法：若套装奖励声明免疫某类效果的 ^green;所有^reset;影响，通常指免疫与该元素相关的所有生物群系天气 ^orange;及^reset;特定状态效果。例如免疫炎热即包含免疫燃烧甚至熔岩；免疫辐射则包含免疫辐射烧伤。\n此外，部分术语或符号用法较为灵活。若奖励显示为 x/y，表示加成依条件满足方式而异；对武器而言，指适用该奖励的武器类型数量。如出现“机枪/手枪”类表述，意为奖励适用于机枪或手枪。此类简写主要为节省提示空间。\n\n^cyan;采矿套装^reset;：\n采矿激光套装能大幅提升采矿激光的伤害...但若同时使用其他类型武器，则该加成会显著降低。例如，同时使用采矿激光与手枪时，2 倍采矿激光伤害加成会降至 1.25 倍。\n^orange;颜色^reset;：颜色对识别和理解奖励效果非常重要。首先，套装奖励通过 ^yellow;^reset; 标识，而 ^green;^reset; 仅在制作界面可见，用于显示抗性。若奖励属性显示为 ^green;绿色^reset;，表示其为增益；^red;红色^reset; 表示减益；^cyan;青色^reset; 则代表二元性效果。同类效果通常无法叠加，这一点在各种食物上尤为明显...请谨慎选择。需注意颜色规则有一个例外：发光。若“发光”字样带有颜色，通常表示该发光效果的颜色。\n\n^orange;特殊奖励^reset;：部分套装拥有特殊奖励，但由于空间限制，装备提示无法显示完整信息。这是游戏的一个不幸的局限性。以下将解释部分奖励词条：\n\n^cyan;自适应护甲^reset;：根据当前生命值百分比（20%时为左侧数值，100%时为右侧数值）按比例提升穿戴者的总防御力。\n\n^cyan;自动医疗^reset;：比普通回复更复杂，此效果每秒恢复更多生命值，但消耗等比例的能量，同时以治疗百分比的两倍降低能量回复并延长能量回复延迟。\n\n^cyan;荆棘^reset;：受击时释放荆棘新星；^cyan;火焰爆裂^reset;则替换为火焰新星。\n\n^cyan;召唤仆从^reset;：召唤短暂存在的盟友协同作战或吸引敌人。仆从强度取决于套装中最低等级护甲，因此升级全部部件至关重要！\n\n^cyan;生命/能量护盾^reset;：获得基于最大资源（生命值/能量）的伤害吸收护盾。若近期未受伤害，护盾将快速恢复。^cyan;护盾免疫^reset;仅在护盾存在时生效。数值依次表示：护盾容量相对于资源的比例、恢复速率、受伤后恢复延迟。注：为平衡性，能量护盾最短延迟为0.5秒，最大恢复速率为每秒50%。\n\n^cyan;重力正常化^reset;：个人重力过低时提升，过高时降低，但零重力除外。\n\n^cyan;生力^reset;与^cyan;神像^reset;：套装专属且效果强大，基于另一属性百分比提升当前属性。生力将生命转化为力量，神像将力量转化为生命。\n\n^cyan;不朽决意^reset;：生命值降低时提升防护，最高至指定数值；^cyan;永生决意^reset;则提供生命回复。若套装同时拥有二者，宠物将获得^cyan;永生决意^reset;。\n\n^cyan;暗黑指挥者^reset;/^cyan;驯兽大师^reset;：按所列百分比提升宠物（二者）和船员（仅暗黑指挥者）的伤害、防护、生命值与速度，跳跃能力提升一半数值，生命值每秒恢复六分之一数值。\n\n^cyan;捕捉专家^reset;：宠物数量+1，每2级最低装备等级再+1（最多+2）。搭配背部物品额外+1。完全升级的套装最多可增加5只宠物！\n\n^red;扭力藤毒素^reset;：摄入扭力藤会降低核心属性和受治疗量，并持续损失生命。短时间内摄入越多、生命值越低，效果越严重。若不谨慎使用，可能^red;导致死亡^reset;。\n\n^cyan;魅力^reset;：影响你在空间站与商人议价的能力。魅力越高，交易越有利（银行存款也越丰厚！）。\n\n\n\n^cyan;宠物/船员属性继承^reset;：\n宠物将从你角色处继承更多属性（含增益与减益），防御和生命值有特定换算比例。整体规则如下：\n生命值：直接基于角色面板计算，不与装备护甲挂钩。\n防御：通过特定公式转化为生命值乘数。\n伤害：直接继承角色面板数值。\n生命回复：除特殊情况（如 ^cyan;不朽决意^reset;、FU未涵盖的加成等）外，以固定数值继承。例如，若你有100点生命值和10%生命回复，宠物每秒将获得10点回复。\n若属性未在此列出，宠物很可能不继承该属性。\n^yellow;特别注意^reset;：使用如 ^cyan;玻璃大炮^reset; 等强力增益时需谨慎，此类效果会显著降低宠物的生命值。"
  }
]